  "id": "fibonacci-stream-skip-grid",
  "title": "Fibonacci streams with conditional key skips",
  "status": "published",
  "record_type": "experiment",
  "question": "Does the complete fixed Fibonacci seed grid clear the source LP2 score gates when conditional key skips are permitted?",
  "summary": "An exact phase/sign reduction turns 925,100 source labels into 92,510 canonical screens.900 settings receive complete-page decoding; none passes the source final gate or the separate retained-terminal normalized audit.",
  "reader_finding": "No full-page result passed the English-score test. The search covered all 841 starting pairs for the specified modulo-29 Fibonacci recurrence.",
  "reader_limit": "Only this Fibonacci recurrence and conditional-skip decoder were tested. Most settings received a 50-rune check; a passing score would not guarantee correct plaintext.",
  "pages_note": "LP2-00 through49 and51 through55; the blank LP2-50 has no rune stream.",
  "bounds_note": "841 canonical seeds x 55 pages x 2 Atbash states =92,510 short screens; equivalent to 925,100 source labels;900 full-page confirmations.",
