  "outcome": "not-supported",
  "finding": "92,510 canonical short settings exactly represent 925,100 source-labeled Fibonacci settings.900 canonical full decodes represent 9,000 labels; none clears strict>-5.5. Best source-returned full score -6.306038765432711. A separately frozen POST-TARGET audit scores 160,613 retained hypotheses:778 settings improve under normalization, but none crosses -5.5; best -6.276971493386715. All 841 plants pass both score gates,805 recover exactly,21 have no skips.",
  "limitations": "Source cumulative beam selection differs from normalized acceptance. All 36 nonexact controls retain the valid true reading in the final beam; four chosen alternatives have worse normalized scores. Controls condition on maximum 3 skips and do not calibrate full-search false positives. Aliases are duplicate settings, not independent evidence. Rejected screens were not fully decoded. No plaintext validation, global p-value, general key-family exclusion or OTP inference.",
  "next_steps": "A distinct proposal should freeze a different key/clock or ranking rule with complete-reading recovery controls and a prospective full-search calibration before manuscript inspection.",
